--- The script itself, refusing a hostile port before it does anything ---
  $ bash tools/start.sh --port '7990|e'
      --port needs a port number, not '7990|e'
    exit=2
  $ bash tools/start.sh --port '.*'
      --port needs a port number, not '.*'
    exit=2
  $ bash tools/start.sh --port '99999'
      --port needs a port between 1 and 65535, not '99999'
    exit=2
  (With the pre-fix script these reached the Caddyfile generator, which is the first section of the
   probe: '7990|e' makes sed fail with 'bad flag in substitute command', '.*' writes the site address
   as 'http://:.*', and '&' splices the matched text back into the config.)

