--- What each mutation shows ---
M1 and M2 remove the validation from one option each: the probe's source check fails — "the option loop does
not call it" — which is the half that the extracted function cannot see, since it is still refusing when
called directly. M3 drops the range check: 0 and 99999 are accepted. M4 refuses a valid port as well: the
counterweight fails, which is why it is there — a check that only forbids hostile values would be happy with
a script that rejects every port.

